# Example requests for the VS Code "REST Client" extension.
# Every request needs a session: send "Login" in auth.http first.
# Replace the category ids with ids of your own EXPENSE categories (GET /categories).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api
@categoryId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Budgets of a month, each with what has been spent in its category (CONFIRMED expenses only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/budgets?month=2026-11

### Create a budget (amount in cents: 300,00 €)
# @name created
POST {{baseUrl}}/budgets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "categoryId": "{{categoryId}}",
  "amount": 30000,
  "month": "2026-11"
}

### Change its amount (only the amount can change)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/budgets/{{created.response.body.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 35000
}

### Delete it (204 No Content)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/budgets/{{created.response.body.id}}

### Copy the budgets of the previous month (2026-10) into 2026-11.
# Categories that already have a budget in 2026-11 keep theirs. Returns { "copied": N }
POST {{baseUrl}}/budgets/copy
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "month": "2026-11"
}


### ---------- Error cases ----------

### 400: `month` is required
GET {{baseUrl}}/budgets

### 400: an INCOME category cannot have a budget (use the id of one of your income categories)
POST {{baseUrl}}/budgets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "categoryId": "{{categoryId}}",
  "amount": 1000,
  "month": "2026-11"
}

### 409: send "Create a budget" twice. One budget per category and month
POST {{baseUrl}}/budgets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "categoryId": "{{categoryId}}",
  "amount": 1000,
  "month": "2026-11"
}

### 404: a budget that does not exist (or belongs to another user)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/budgets/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 1000
}
